    "answer": {
      "short": "a and e; b and g; c and h; d and f.",
      "worked": "Since $Z$ is continuous, including an endpoint does not change a probability.\n\n a and e: $P(Z\\le 2)=P(Z<2)\\approx0.9772$.\n\n b and g, by symmetry:\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le-1)&=P(Z\\ge1)\\\\&=1-P(Z\\le1)\\\\&\\approx1-0.8413\\\\&=0.1587.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n c and h, by symmetry: $P(Z\\le1.2)=P(Z>-1.2)\\approx0.8849$.\n\n d and f: $P(Z=4)=P(Z=2.3)=0$, since a continuous random variable has zero probability of taking any single value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
